{
  "_": [
    "Which rung each ## Approach section teaches, in document order.",
    "",
    "This is the ONE judgement call in converting a teaching document, and it is",
    "the only thing in the conversion a machine should not guess: the heading says",
    "'Floyd's tortoise and hare' and the record says 'floyd', and on a journeyed",
    "problem the ladder's keys come from the journey's ACT keys, not from",
    "alternatives[].key at all.",
    "",
    "It lives in a file because the converter is re-runnable: a converter bug means",
    "re-emitting every module, and hand-binding 82 documents twice is how the",
    "second pass gets a different answer from the first. `md-to-content.mjs` reads",
    "this and fills `rung` from it; anything absent is emitted blank and fails",
    "src/content/content.test.ts until a human decides.",
    "",
    "The first twelve below were decided by an agent on 2026-09-14 and are",
    "reproduced from its report. inorder-walk is deliberately out of ladder order:",
    "the document's third approach IS the problem's top-level approach, and Morris",
    "threading sits below optimal rather than above it.",
    "",
    "A `null` entry is an approach the LADDER DOES NOT CARRY — the document",
    "teaches it and the record has no rung for it. `lib/doc-sections.ts` leaves",
    "those sections whole, under their own heading, instead of folding them into",
    "a rung that does not exist. contains-duplicate is the first: its document",
    "teaches five approaches against three rungs, and promoting the other two",
    "needs Java and C++ for each (problems.test.ts), which is a separate branch."
  ],
